# DRAFT: nothing has been released yet. The preferred citation is the dataset's version
# 0.1.0; the release date and the DOI are filled in at release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PlainPairs, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PlainPairs: a research corpus pairing the prescriber and patient texts of US medicine labels"
abstract: >-
  PlainPairs is a research corpus of how United States medicine labels are worded for two
  readers: for every medicine whose label carries a version written for patients (a Medication
  Guide or a patient package insert), the text written for prescribers next to the text written
  for patients, matched by section, with reading-level and plain-language measures on both
  sides. It is a record of wording, not medical information.
authors:
  - family-names: Kraishan
    given-names: Obada
    affiliation: "College of Media and Communication, Texas Tech University"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/obadaKraishan/plainpairs"
keywords:
  - health literacy
  - health communication
  - risk communication
  - readability
  - plain language
  - medication guides
  - dataset
